{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAorsQyUS2wi6YNA9DMa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PnE3kD4CdY9tAEbz7ywHaw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-UwETvo; python3 - <<'E'\np='bin/nightly-review.zsh'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''claude -p \"$PROMPT\" --output-format text > \"$OUT\"\nstatus=$?\n\nif [ $status -ne 0 ]; then\n  \"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review FAILED (exit $status), see $OUT\"\n  exit $status\nfi\n''','''ERR=\"${OUT%.md}.err\"\nclaude -p \"$PROMPT\" --output-format text > \"$OUT\" 2> \"$ERR\"\nrc=$?   # not \"status\": it is read-only in zsh\n\nif [ $rc -ne 0 ]; then\n  \"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review FAILED (exit $rc): $(head -c 200 \"$ERR\")\"\n  exit $rc\nfi\n''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='bin/notify.sh'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('curl -sS -X','curl -sS --fail-with-body -X')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Why the nightly job never reported anything\n\n1. **`claude` is not logged in in the launchd context.** Every run in\n   `nightly-review.err` says `Not logged in · Please run /login`, so the review\n   itself fails every night (`last exit code = 1`, `runs = 6`). Interactive\n   login state is not available to the launchd job. This one I could not fix\n   from here: run `claude setup-token` and provide the token to the job\n   (e.g. `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` in the plist's `EnvironmentVariables`, or\n   read it from the keychain in the script), then reload the agent.\n\n2. **The failure handler crashed, so no failure note was ever sent.** The\n   script did `status=$?`, but `status` is a read-only special variable in zsh\n   (`read-only variable: status`, err line 2 of each run). The script aborted\n   before reaching the `notify.sh` call. Fixed: renamed to `rc`.\n\n3. **The failure message pointed at an empty file and hid the real error.**\n   stderr went to launchd's log, while `$OUT` was empty. Now stderr is saved\n   to `nightly-review-DATE.err` and its first 200 bytes go into the note.\n\n4. **`notify.sh` could fail silently.** `curl -sS` exits 0 on Telegram HTTP\n   errors (bad token/chat) and output goes to /dev/null. Changed to\n   `--fail-with-body` so a rejected message produces a non-zero exit and an\n   error on stderr (visible in `nightly-review.err`).\n\nNote: the plist's PATH (`/opt/homebrew/bin:...`) is fine if `claude` lives\nthere; if it is installed elsewhere (e.g. `~/.local/bin`), add that dir to the\nplist PATH too. After editing, reload with `launchctl bootout` / `bootstrap`.\nE\ngit status --short"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2939,"cache_read_input_tokens":20441,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2939},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8761388-675e-4398-ac93-51b9f6f247a2","uuid":"85afec97-8b18-46f4-9670-b901b4b84273","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:29:54.523Z","request_id":"req_011CgAors77V4XMVXfhf9sgy","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PnE3kD4CdY9tAEbz7ywHaw":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-UwETvo; python3 - <<'E'\np='bin/nightly-review.zsh'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''claude -p \"$PROMPT\" --output-format text > \"$OUT\"\nstatus=$?\n\nif [ $status -ne 0 ]; then\n  \"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review FAILED (exit $status), see $OUT\"\n  exit $status\nfi\n''','''ERR=\"${OUT%.md}.err\"\nclaude -p \"$PROMPT\" --output-format text > \"$OUT\" 2> \"$ERR\"\nrc=$?   # not \"status\": it is read-only in zsh\n\nif [ $rc -ne 0 ]; then\n  \"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review FAILED (exit $rc): $(head -c 200 \"$ERR\")\"\n  exit $rc\nfi\n''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='bin/notify.sh'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('curl -sS -X','curl -sS --fail-with-body -X')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Why the nightly job never reported anything\n\n1. **`claude` is not logged in in the launchd context.** Every run in\n   `nightly-review.err` says `Not logged in · Please run /login`, so the review\n   itself fails every night (`last exit code = 1`, `runs = 6`). Interactive\n   login state is not available to the launchd job. This one I could not fix\n   from here: run `claude setup-token` and provide the token to the job\n   (e.g. `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` in the plist's `EnvironmentVariables`, or\n   read it from the keychain in the script), then reload the agent.\n\n2. **The failure handler crashed, so no failure note was ever sent.** The\n   script did `status=$?`, but `status` is a read-only special variable in zsh\n   (`read-only variable: status`, err line 2 of each run). The script aborted\n   before reaching the `notify.sh` call. Fixed: renamed to `rc`.\n\n3. **The failure message pointed at an empty file and hid the real error.**\n   stderr went to launchd's log, while `$OUT` was empty. Now stderr is saved\n   to `nightly-review-DATE.err` and its first 200 bytes go into the note.\n\n4. **`notify.sh` could fail silently.** `curl -sS` exits 0 on Telegram HTTP\n   errors (bad token/chat) and output goes to /dev/null. Changed to\n   `--fail-with-body` so a rejected message produces a non-zero exit and an\n   error on stderr (visible in `nightly-review.err`).\n\nNote: the plist's PATH (`/opt/homebrew/bin:...`) is fine if `claude` lives\nthere; if it is installed elsewhere (e.g. `~/.local/bin`), add that dir to the\nplist PATH too. After editing, reload with `launchctl bootout` / `bootstrap`.\nE\ngit status --short"}}}
