{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAosfQCRaaa8c4zx4E42","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job has been failing every night, and the script broke before it could tell you. I haven't run any of it, and I haven't fixed the login problem. I can't do that from here.\n\n1. **Not logged in (not fixed):** `claude` can't log in when launchd runs it. All six runs in `nightly-review.err` say `Not logged in · Please run /login`, and `launchctl print` shows `last exit code = 1`. To fix it, run `claude setup-token` and give the job the token. You could put `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` in the plist or read it from the keychain in the script. Then reload the agent.\n2. **Failure note never sent (fixed):** the script did `status=$?`, but `status` is read-only in zsh. The script aborted with `read-only variable: status` before it reached `notify.sh`. I renamed the variable to `rc`.\n3. **Failure note pointed at an empty file (fixed):** stderr now goes to `nightly-review-DATE.err`, and the first 200 bytes of it are in the Telegram note.\n4. **Silent Telegram errors (fixed):** `curl -sS` exits 0 even when Telegram rejects the message. I changed it to `--fail-with-body`, so a rejected message now shows up in the error log.\n\nI couldn't check where `claude` is installed. If it isn't in `/opt/homebrew/bin` or `/usr/local/bin`, add its directory to the plist `PATH`.\n\nThe causes are written up in `ANSWER.md`. The script edits are in `bin/nightly-review.zsh` and `bin/notify.sh`. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1551,"cache_read_input_tokens":23380,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1551},"output_tokens":541,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"p